WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.200
SmartVest Investing Academy.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.625
Lesson 6: Why Long-Term Investing?

3
00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:16.300
If you follow daily financial headlines, you might believe that investing is about buying and selling every day to predict market tops and bottoms.

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.137
But what does historical evidence actually show?

5
00:00:20.137 --> 00:00:27.200
History consistently demonstrates that the most successful wealth builders are long-term investors.

6
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:36.163
Long-term investing means committing your capital to quality assets for time horizons of 5, 10, 15 years or more.

7
00:00:36.163 --> 00:00:45.362
In the short term, financial markets are driven by emotion, news events, geopolitical tension, and speculative sentiment.

8
00:00:45.362 --> 00:00:50.350
Over days or months, market prices can swing unpredictably.

9
00:00:50.350 --> 00:01:01.400
However, over multi-year horizons, stock markets reflect the fundamental earnings power, innovation, and economic productivity of underlying businesses.

10
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:13.600
Consider market history: over any random 1-year holding period, stock market returns can be highly volatile, swinging between positive 30% and negative 20%.

11
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:27.587
But as you extend your investment horizon to 7, 10, or 15 years in diversified market indices, the probability of achieving positive real returns has historically approached 100%.

12
00:01:27.588 --> 00:01:46.250
Long-term investing also offers massive structural advantages: you save significantly on brokerage fees, you avoid high short-term capital gains taxes, and most importantly, you eliminate the emotional stress of trying to time unpredictable daily market noise.

13
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:53.062
A common mistake is believing long-term investing means buying a stock and ignoring it blindly forever.

14
00:01:53.062 --> 00:02:02.912
Sound investing involves patience with the market, combined with annual reviews to ensure your asset allocation remains aligned with your goals.

15
00:02:02.912 --> 00:02:10.050
Keep in mind that holding a single failing company for the long term will not save it from poor fundamentals.

16
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:15.200
Long-term patience must always be paired with broad diversification.

17
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:24.375
Time in the market consistently beats timing the market; patient discipline allows economic growth and compounding to create lasting wealth.

18
00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:27.425
SmartVest Investing Academy.

19
00:02:27.425 --> 00:02:29.250
Learn first.

20
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.700
Invest with understanding.
